OL,3,CWhat does Nigel Farage's by-election
OL,4,Cwin mean for probe into his finances?
OL,6,FIn total 34 candidates stood in the
OL,7,FClacton by-election, making it the
OL,8,Fmost contested seat in British history.
OL,10,FThe absence, however, of any other
OL,11,Fcredible opposition meant comedy
OL,12,Fcandidate Count Binface, who has stood
OL,13,Fin multiple high-profile elections,
OL,14,Fbecame Farage's strongest opponent.
OL,16,FWhen the results were announced,
OL,17,FFarage won 22,239 votes - 63% of the
OL,18,Ftotal.
OL,20,FCount Binface won 9,455 - 27%.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/14
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
